==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|putten}}, {{m|enm|puten}}, {{m|enm|poten}}, from {{inh|en|ang|putian}}, {{m|ang|*pūtian}} {{gloss|"to push, put out"; attested by derivative {{m|ang|putung||pushing, impulse, instigation, urging}}}} and {{m|ang|potian||to push, thrust, strike, butt, goad}}, both from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*putōną||to stick, stab}}, which is of uncertain origin. Possibly from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bud-||to shoot, sprout}}, which would make it cognate with {{cog|sa|बुन्द||tr=bundá|arrow}}, {{cog|lt|budė}}, and {{m|lt|budis||mushroom, fungus}}. Compare also related {{cog|ang|pȳtan||to push, poke, thrust, put out (the eyes)}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|poten||to set, plant}}, {{cog|da|putte||to put}}, {{cog|sv|putta}}, {{m|sv|pötta}}, {{m|sv|potta||to strike, knock, push gently, shove, put away}}, {{cog|no|putte||to set, put}}, {{cog|no|pota||to poke}}, {{cog|is|pota||to poke}}, {{cog|nl|peuteren||to pick, poke around, dig, fiddle with}}.

